{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YDVxfKsor9ppHkNWCV8T3v","type":"tool_result","content":"GitHub labels, all prefixed `ard:`, are the queue and the state machine. `.ard/<issue#>/` is the shared working memory and audit log, and `.ard/<type>/<name>/` holds each role's prompt and runtime by convention.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    S[\"Scanners<br/>every X h; dedupe by fingerprint, group up to N\"] -->|ard:pending| T[\"Triage<br/>lead routes to PM, architect, designer, docs, eng\"]\n    T -->|\"ard:triage:ROLE:done\"| G{\"All triage done<br/>and ard:approved?\"}\n    G -->|\"ard:worker:ROLE\"| W[\"Worker<br/>branch, code, test, draft PR\"]\n    W -->|\"ard:review:ROLE on the PR\"| R[\"Reviewers<br/>security, license, eng, PM\"]\n    R -->|\"ard:review:ROLE:changes (max 3 rounds)\"| W\n    R -->|\"all reviews done, checks green\"| M[\"Merger<br/>squash-merge closes the issue\"]\n    subgraph ctl[\"ard controller, one per repo\"]\n        P[\"Poll loops: fill slots, reviewers first\"]\n        E[\"Executors: max 3 pods, local or k8s\"]\n        A[\"Agent adapters: claude, kimi, dsh-tui\"]\n        C[\"Committer: sole writer to main\"]\n        X[\"Reaper: ard:executor:failed, keep 24 h\"]\n        D[\"State: controller db plus one SQLite db per scanner\"]\n    end\n```\n\nEach arrow is a label the controller sets at close-out; dashed lines show the stages it runs. A reviewer's `changes` verdict sends the PR back to the worker, at most three times; once every review passes, the merger lands it.\n\n## Stack\n\n19:func TestCheckCommandsFixtures(t *testing.T) {\n35:\t\tgot, err := CheckCommands(one(c.body), paths)\n46:func TestCheckKeysFixtures(t *testing.T) {\n48:\tgot, _ := CheckKeys(one(\"| `max_pods` | 3 |\\n| `old_key` | x |\\n\"), \"a.md\", keys)\n54:\tif got, _ := CheckKeys(one(\"| `max_pods` |\\n| `paused` |\\n\"), \"a.md\", keys); len(got) != 0 {\n77:\tproblems, err := CheckCommands(os.DirFS(siteDir(t)), cli.CommandPaths())\n87:\tproblems, err := CheckKeys(os.DirFS(siteDir(t)), \"configuration.md\", config.Keys())","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed7477ba-cac6-485b-abc4-7f4a7f16a93c","uuid":"86ce1a19-5736-4118-afd7-cac9c7fc6b7e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T12:28:05.469Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"GitHub labels, all prefixed `ard:`, are the queue and the state machine. `.ard/<issue#>/` is the shared working memory and audit log, and `.ard/<type>/<name>/` holds each role's prompt and runtime by convention.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    S[\"Scanners<br/>every X h; dedupe by fingerprint, group up to N\"] -->|ard:pending| T[\"Triage<br/>lead routes to PM, architect, designer, docs, eng\"]\n    T -->|\"ard:triage:ROLE:done\"| G{\"All triage done<br/>and ard:approved?\"}\n    G -->|\"ard:worker:ROLE\"| W[\"Worker<br/>branch, code, test, draft PR\"]\n    W -->|\"ard:review:ROLE on the PR\"| R[\"Reviewers<br/>security, license, eng, PM\"]\n    R -->|\"ard:review:ROLE:changes (max 3 rounds)\"| W\n    R -->|\"all reviews done, checks green\"| M[\"Merger<br/>squash-merge closes the issue\"]\n    subgraph ctl[\"ard controller, one per repo\"]\n        P[\"Poll loops: fill slots, reviewers first\"]\n        E[\"Executors: max 3 pods, local or k8s\"]\n        A[\"Agent adapters: claude, kimi, dsh-tui\"]\n        C[\"Committer: sole writer to main\"]\n        X[\"Reaper: ard:executor:failed, keep 24 h\"]\n        D[\"State: controller db plus one SQLite db per scanner\"]\n    end\n```\n\nEach arrow is a label the controller sets at close-out; dashed lines show the stages it runs. A reviewer's `changes` verdict sends the PR back to the worker, at most three times; once every review passes, the merger lands it.\n\n## Stack\n\n19:func TestCheckCommandsFixtures(t *testing.T) {\n35:\t\tgot, err := CheckCommands(one(c.body), paths)\n46:func TestCheckKeysFixtures(t *testing.T) {\n48:\tgot, _ := CheckKeys(one(\"| `max_pods` | 3 |\\n| `old_